.TH CHTTP_BASE64_DECODE_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_decode_mp \- base64-decode a string with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

void *chttp_base64_decode_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp,
                             const char *b64_input, size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Decodes a NUL-terminated standard RFC 4648 base64 string (the '+'/'/'
alphabet, '=' padding). The input length is taken from
strlen(b64_input); it must be a multiple of 4 bytes, and any '='
padding must appear only as the final one or two characters. Any
other malformed input (invalid character, misplaced padding, wrong
length) is rejected.

The returned buffer is NUL-terminated as a convenience for decoding
text payloads, but the decoded data may legitimately contain embedded
NUL bytes; always use out_len, never strlen(), to determine its
real size.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mp         Custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
b64_input  NUL-terminated base64 string to decode. Must not be NULL.
out_len    Optional; receives the decoded byte length. Pass NULL to
           ignore.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Newly allocated decoded buffer on success.
NULL on allocation failure or malformed input.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_decode (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_basic_auth_mp (3)
